WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.396 --> 00:00:01.872
Nine at night.

2
00:00:02.096 --> 00:00:03.381
An empty pitch.

3
00:00:03.726 --> 00:00:07.767
Just you, one ball, and
a keeper in your head.

4
00:00:08.217 --> 00:00:09.281
His name is Chalk.

5
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.020
You draw one line around the ball.

6
00:00:12.424 --> 00:00:13.407
Remember that line.

7
00:00:14.143 --> 00:00:14.920
You shoot.

8
00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:17.703
Over the bar.

9
00:00:18.736 --> 00:00:19.636
You shout at it.

10
00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:21.174
It doesn't listen.

11
00:00:22.003 --> 00:00:23.582
Chalk doesn't even move.

12
00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:25.625
What went wrong?

13
00:00:25.902 --> 00:00:29.267
Your foot touches the ball for
about a hundredth of a second.

14
00:00:29.475 --> 00:00:31.382
After that, it's on its own.

15
00:00:31.665 --> 00:00:34.961
Three kicks tonight, one idea: spin.

16
00:00:35.406 --> 00:00:38.121
How much, which way, or none at all.

17
00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:40.912
By lights out, you'll score this shot.

18
00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:46.742
Problem one: a shot Chalk can't reach.

19
00:00:46.918 --> 00:00:49.721
Low and hard.

20
00:00:49.811 --> 00:00:53.469
Weird fact: after a clean strike, the
ball can fly faster than your foot.

21
00:00:53.865 --> 00:00:54.490
How?

22
00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.898
First, the whip.

23
00:00:57.084 --> 00:01:01.285
Your thigh swings, slows,
and flings your shin forward.

24
00:01:01.789 --> 00:01:03.312
Then, the trampoline.

25
00:01:03.539 --> 00:01:06.294
The ball squashes and springs back.

26
00:01:06.715 --> 00:01:10.527
Your leg is way heavier, so the ball
bounces off faster than your foot.

27
00:01:11.066 --> 00:01:14.681
Club players your age shoot about
sixty-seven kilometres an hour.

28
00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:19.471
A floppy ankle is a
hammer with a loose head.

29
00:01:19.511 --> 00:01:21.157
Some of the hit leaks away.

30
00:01:21.343 --> 00:01:22.892
So: toes down, ankle locked.

31
00:01:22.932 --> 00:01:24.264
Hit with the middle of your laces.

32
00:01:24.561 --> 00:01:26.134
That's your instep.

33
00:01:26.174 --> 00:01:31.057
Hit near your toes, and it's
about fifteen percent slower.

34
00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:36.591
Your foot swings like a playground
swing, flat only at the bottom.

35
00:01:36.874 --> 00:01:37.888
Meet the ball there.

36
00:01:38.287 --> 00:01:42.206
So put your standing foot beside
the ball, toes at the goal.

37
00:01:42.849 --> 00:01:45.973
Put it behind, and your
kicking foot is already rising.

38
00:01:46.577 --> 00:01:47.996
Hello, car alarm.

39
00:01:48.036 --> 00:01:50.398
Kicking knee and chest over the ball.

40
00:01:50.517 --> 00:01:51.492
Eyes on it.

41
00:01:51.732 --> 00:01:53.186
Strike through the middle.

42
00:01:53.622 --> 00:01:57.260
The line turns slowly
backward: a little backspin.

43
00:01:58.412 --> 00:02:02.037
Classic mistake: toes up,
so the ball hits your toes.

44
00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:05.762
Point your toes down, lock
your ankle, then swing.

45
00:02:06.161 --> 00:02:09.243
Solo drill: tape a line
across a wall at knee height.

46
00:02:09.426 --> 00:02:12.002
From ten big steps, shoot ten under it.

47
00:02:12.042 --> 00:02:13.184
Start at half power.

48
00:02:13.352 --> 00:02:14.578
Now, for real.

49
00:02:14.837 --> 00:02:15.831
Chalk dives.

50
00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:16.722
Too late.

51
00:02:17.849 --> 00:02:18.789
Problem two.

52
00:02:19.092 --> 00:02:21.635
He builds a wall and guards the near post.

53
00:02:21.675 --> 00:02:24.545
You need a ball that
starts wide and bends back.

54
00:02:24.713 --> 00:02:26.105
You need sideways spin.

55
00:02:27.053 --> 00:02:28.730
New kick, new rule.

56
00:02:28.979 --> 00:02:30.459
Inside of your foot.

57
00:02:30.515 --> 00:02:36.263
This time, toes up, but the ankle
stays locked: a firm, flat face.

58
00:02:36.725 --> 00:02:38.276
Hit just right of centre.

59
00:02:38.617 --> 00:02:40.557
Wrap your foot around the
ball, out to the right.

60
00:02:40.982 --> 00:02:41.672
Left-footed?

61
00:02:41.746 --> 00:02:42.360
Flip it.

62
00:02:44.181 --> 00:02:46.855
Air rushes past the ball like a crowd.

63
00:02:47.109 --> 00:02:50.566
The spinning ball grabs the
air and flings it to one side.

64
00:02:50.917 --> 00:02:53.183
Throw air one way, get
shoved the other way.

65
00:02:53.515 --> 00:02:55.883
That's the Magnus effect: the spin push.

66
00:02:56.846 --> 00:02:58.732
Curlers seem to bend late.

67
00:02:58.944 --> 00:02:59.574
They don't.

68
00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.671
They bend about the same the whole way.

69
00:03:01.754 --> 00:03:05.516
But the gap from a straight
line grows faster and faster.

70
00:03:05.605 --> 00:03:08.743
From twenty metres, the
gap is almost three metres.

71
00:03:08.783 --> 00:03:11.131
So to the keeper, it looks late.

72
00:03:12.157 --> 00:03:16.233
From twenty metres, aim about
three metres outside the far post.

73
00:03:16.363 --> 00:03:18.057
Point your standing foot there.

74
00:03:18.145 --> 00:03:19.034
Closer to goal?

75
00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:20.150
Aim less wide.

76
00:03:20.689 --> 00:03:22.035
Classic mistake: aiming
straight at the post.

77
00:03:22.171 --> 00:03:25.570
The spin pulls it back to Chalk.

78
00:03:25.933 --> 00:03:29.426
Solo drill: put your
bag halfway to the goal.

79
00:03:29.761 --> 00:03:31.368
Curl ten balls around it.

80
00:03:31.826 --> 00:03:32.796
Starts wide.

81
00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:33.953
Comes home.

82
00:03:35.237 --> 00:03:36.121
Problem three.

83
00:03:36.397 --> 00:03:37.923
Chalk punches it clear.

84
00:03:38.079 --> 00:03:40.110
You pop it up off your thigh.

85
00:03:40.315 --> 00:03:42.369
Now hit it before it lands.

86
00:03:45.928 --> 00:03:48.017
The ball keeps falling while you swing.

87
00:03:48.178 --> 00:03:51.687
So set your standing foot early,
beside where it will drop.

88
00:03:52.088 --> 00:03:53.189
Start your swing early.

89
00:03:53.719 --> 00:03:55.868
Hit it at knee height or lower.

90
00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:58.982
Your instep is a tennis racket.

91
00:03:59.187 --> 00:04:01.321
Toes down, and it tilts forward.

92
00:04:01.603 --> 00:04:04.032
Lean back, and the ball flies over.

93
00:04:04.969 --> 00:04:07.540
The falling ball rolls down your laces.

94
00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.319
That can give it topspin.

95
00:04:09.527 --> 00:04:12.861
It flicks air up, so the
spin push points down.

96
00:04:13.108 --> 00:04:16.423
It dives, up to about a metre
lower than with no spin.

97
00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:18.420
Classic mistake?

98
00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:19.807
Smashing it.

99
00:04:19.943 --> 00:04:22.571
Same angle, but the
harder shot flies over.

100
00:04:22.699 --> 00:04:25.144
It arrives sooner, so it
has less time to fall.

101
00:04:25.184 --> 00:04:27.227
Fix: nose over knee, knee over ball.

102
00:04:27.292 --> 00:04:30.248
Hit the middle, not the bottom.

103
00:04:30.288 --> 00:04:31.532
Clean beats hard.

104
00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:36.104
Solo drill: drop the ball
three big steps from a wall.

105
00:04:36.223 --> 00:04:37.332
Let it bounce once.

106
00:04:37.521 --> 00:04:39.005
Volley it at the top,
where it almost stops.

107
00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:40.798
Start soft.

108
00:04:41.159 --> 00:04:42.001
Stay under the tape.

109
00:04:42.041 --> 00:04:43.003
Now, for real.

110
00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:45.954
Under the bar.

111
00:04:46.964 --> 00:04:48.828
Bonus kick: the chip.

112
00:04:49.038 --> 00:04:50.952
Same air, opposite spin.

113
00:04:51.076 --> 00:04:54.884
Jab your laces under the ball,
a thumb's width above the grass.

114
00:04:54.924 --> 00:04:56.040
Then stop your foot.

115
00:04:56.531 --> 00:05:01.843
It pops up steep with backspin, flicks
air down, and hangs over a rushing keeper.

116
00:05:02.909 --> 00:05:04.383
That first shot tonight?

117
00:05:04.828 --> 00:05:06.489
Your foot came up under it.

118
00:05:06.957 --> 00:05:10.315
It took off steep, with
backspin, like a chip.

119
00:05:10.727 --> 00:05:11.848
By accident.

120
00:05:12.304 --> 00:05:14.585
Chip on purpose, when
the keeper rushes out.

121
00:05:18.061 --> 00:05:19.459
The first shot again.

122
00:05:19.546 --> 00:05:21.613
Standing foot beside the ball.

123
00:05:21.829 --> 00:05:23.771
Toes down, ankle locked.

124
00:05:23.896 --> 00:05:24.519
Low.

125
00:05:24.559 --> 00:05:25.189
Hard.

126
00:05:25.311 --> 00:05:25.842
In.

127
00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:27.447
No shouting needed.

128
00:05:28.544 --> 00:05:32.252
And that line?

129
00:05:32.428 --> 00:05:33.771
It told you everything.

130
00:05:34.046 --> 00:05:36.987
A little backspin, hard and low: speed.

131
00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:38.935
Sideways: bend.

132
00:05:39.265 --> 00:05:41.100
Topspin: dive.

133
00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:43.981
Backspin, soft and high: float.

134
00:05:44.733 --> 00:05:47.457
What if the line hardly turns?

135
00:05:47.873 --> 00:05:50.461
A knuckleball turns
less than once a second.

136
00:05:50.581 --> 00:05:54.300
The air behind it flaps like
a flag, and the ball zigzags.

137
00:05:54.516 --> 00:05:56.066
Chalk has no idea.

138
00:05:56.667 --> 00:05:57.635
Neither do you.

139
00:05:58.289 --> 00:05:59.444
Nail the drive first.

140
00:05:59.748 --> 00:06:01.514
Then come back for the knuckleball.

141
00:06:02.435 --> 00:06:03.509
Half past nine.

142
00:06:03.735 --> 00:06:04.490
Lights out.

143
00:06:05.013 --> 00:06:07.830
Your foot gets about a hundredth
of a second with the ball.

144
00:06:09.126 --> 00:06:10.802
Now you know how to spend it.
